      "title": "Easy Sandboxing on Linux with Bubblewrap",
      "url": "https://bxt.rs/blog/easy-sandboxing-on-linux-with-bubblewrap/",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/stehhb",
      "score": 2,
      "comments": 1,
      "author": "FedericoSchonborn",
      "published": "2026-08-10T10:37:20Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Bubblewrap (bwrap) leverages unprivileged Linux user and mount namespaces to isolate untrusted processes without requiring setuid root privileges.",
        "Restricts attack surfaces by creating minimal filesystem views with bind-mounts, disabling network access via --unshare-net, and isolating IPC/PID namespaces.",
        "Integrates with Seccomp-BPF filters to enforce strict syscall restrictions, providing a lightweight, low-overhead alternative to full container runtimes."
      ]
    },
